  partName: Engine Block (3)
  description: The Engine Block (3) is a small, complex component located at the
    middle-center-center of the jet engine, serving as the main structural element
    of the engine. Its accent-yellow material is chosen for its high visibility,
    making it easier to inspect and maintain. Notably, the engine block's compact
    size and complex shape allow for a high power-to-weight ratio, making it suitable
    for jet engine applications.
